{
  "duration": 61.459,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.979,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.5,
      "end": 2.639,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.259,
      "end": 4.019,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.619,
      "end": 7.419,
      "text": "we are given that two runners are five hundred meter apart."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.98,
      "end": 10.319,
      "text": "The first runner is running at six meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.859,
      "end": 13.139,
      "text": "The second runner is running at four meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.779,
      "end": 15.659,
      "text": "Also, they are running towards each other."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.199,
      "end": 19.199,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find after how many seconds they will meet."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.619,
      "end": 21.579,
      "text": "Now, let us understand one important concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.0,
      "end": 24.34,
      "text": "When two objects move towards each other,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.76,
      "end": 27.659,
      "text": "the distance between them keeps reducing from both sides."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.079,
      "end": 28.879,
      "text": "So in this case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.34,
      "end": 31.059,
      "text": "we do not subtract the speeds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.559,
      "end": 32.199,
      "text": "we add them."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.639,
      "end": 36.54,
      "text": "And we add the speeds only because they are moving towards each other. Got it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.02,
      "end": 37.419,
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.819,
      "end": 40.639,
      "text": "So the relative speed is equal to the sum of their speeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.059,
      "end": 45.879,
      "text": "Relative speed equals six plus four equals ten meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.36,
      "end": 47.359,
      "text": "Now we know the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.899,
      "end": 51.039,
      "text": "Time is equal to distance divided by relative speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.52,
      "end": 52.459,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.799,
      "end": 55.139,
      "text": "time equals five hundred divided by ten,"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.659,
      "end": 56.699,
      "text": "which is fifty seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.0,
      "end": 59.299,
      "text": "So the two runners will meet after fifty seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.639,
      "end": 61.459,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option A."
    }
  ],
